IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`
IMPORT `ssc3-a0-s61za-s61zc`
IMPORT `ssc3-a-s43-s44`

-- Tests for ssc3-helpers.l4, ssc3-a0-s61za-s61zc.l4 (ss 61ZA to 61ZC) and ssc3-a-s43-s44.l4 (ss 43, 44).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it; none is copied from the encoding's output.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A Person
`a person attaining pensionable age on` MEANS
    Person WITH
        `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
        `sex` IS Woman
        `marital status` IS `married`
        `date of attaining pensionable age` IS day

`A pension at 100` MEANS `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category A retirement pension`, "A", 100, FALSE, FALSE
`A pension at 20 because of 61ZA` MEANS `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category A retirement pension`, "A61", 20, TRUE, FALSE
`B pension at 80` MEANS `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category B retirement pension`, "B-spouse", 80, FALSE, FALSE
`B pension at 120` MEANS `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category B retirement pension`, "B-widow", 120, FALSE, FALSE
`B pension at 30 because of 61ZB` MEANS `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category B retirement pension`, "B61", 30, FALSE, TRUE
`C pension at 60` MEANS `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category C retirement pension`, "C", 60, FALSE, FALSE
`D pension at 70` MEANS `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category D retirement pension`, "D", 70, FALSE, FALSE

`the week commencing on 8 January 2024` MEANS Date 8 1 2024
`notice for B-spouse dated 7 January 2024` MEANS `s 43 Notice` OF "B-spouse", Date 7 1 2024
`notice for B-spouse dated 8 January 2024` MEANS `s 43 Notice` OF "B-spouse", Date 8 1 2024
`notice for B-widow dated 1 January 2024` MEANS `s 43 Notice` OF "B-widow", Date 1 1 2024
`notice for A dated 1 January 2024` MEANS `s 43 Notice` OF "A", Date 1 1 2024
`notice for C dated 1 January 2024` MEANS `s 43 Notice` OF "C", Date 1 1 2024
`notice for a pension nobody has` MEANS `s 43 Notice` OF "Z", Date 1 1 2024

§ `Helpers: three-valued logic (no section; the departure is recorded in NOTES.md)`

-- all of: FALSE wins over NOTHING; NOTHING wins over TRUE; the empty list is TRUE.
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper all of` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper all of` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper all of` (LIST NOTHING, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper all of` (LIST NOTHING, JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper all of` EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- any of: TRUE wins over NOTHING; NOTHING wins over FALSE; the empty list is FALSE.
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper any of` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper any of` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper any of` (LIST NOTHING, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper any of` (LIST NOTHING, JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper any of` EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper not` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper not` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper known` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- tax year beginning 6 April: 5 April 2016 is in the year that began in 2015, 6 April 2016 in the year that began in 2016.
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper tax year of` (Date 5 4 2016) EQUALS 2015
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper tax year of` (Date 6 4 2016) EQUALS 2016
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper tax year of` (Date 1 1 2017) EQUALS 2016
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper tax year of` (Date 31 12 2016) EQUALS 2016
#ASSERT `ssc3 helper first day of tax year` 1999 EQUALS Date 6 4 1999

§ `Section 61ZA: people with units of additional pension`

-- (1): applies to a person with one or more units, not entitled to a Category A pension, who would be if the conditions were satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` 2 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` 1 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` 0 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` 2 TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` 2 FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` 2 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person` 0 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): the conditions are taken to be satisfied where (1) applies; otherwise the text is silent.
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the only element is the additional pension attributable to the units.
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(3) the weekly rate of the pension the person is entitled to because of section 61ZA` TRUE 12.5 EQUALS JUST 12.5
#ASSERT `s 61ZA(3) the weekly rate of the pension the person is entitled to because of section 61ZA` FALSE 12.5 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 61ZB: people whose dead spouse had units of additional pension`

#ASSERT `s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person` 3 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person` 0 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person` 3 TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person` 3 FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person` 3 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(3) the weekly rate of the pension the person is entitled to because of section 61ZB` TRUE 7.25 EQUALS JUST 7.25
#ASSERT `s 61ZB(3) the weekly rate of the pension the person is entitled to because of section 61ZB` FALSE 7.25 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 61ZC: entitlement to more than one pension`

#ASSERT `s 61ZC(1) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` TRUE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(1) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` TRUE 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(1) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(1) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` FALSE 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(2) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` TRUE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(2) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(2) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` FALSE 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(3)(a) section 43(2)(a) includes a Category A and a Category B retirement pension` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(3)(a) section 43(2)(a) includes a Category A and a Category B retirement pension` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(3)(a) section 43(2)(a) includes a Category A and a Category B retirement pension` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(3)(a) section 43(2)(a) includes a Category A and a Category B retirement pension` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(3)(b) the pension counts as a Category A retirement pension in sections 43(3)(a) and (aa), 51A and 52` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(3)(b) the pension counts as a Category A retirement pension in sections 43(3)(a) and (aa), 51A and 52` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(3)(c) the pension counts as a Category B retirement pension in sections 43(3)(a) and 52` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61ZC(3)(c) the pension counts as a Category B retirement pension in sections 43(3)(a) and 52` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 43: more than one retirement pension`

-- (6): a pension under section 55A or 55AA is not a retirement pension.
#ASSERT `s 43(6) the pension is a retirement pension for the purposes of section 43` `shared additional pension` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 43(6) the pension is a retirement pension for the purposes of section 43` `Category A retirement pension` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 43(6) the pension is a retirement pension for the purposes of section 43` `Category D retirement pension` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 43(6) the pension is a retirement pension for the purposes of section 43` `attendance allowance` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1): one pension for the same period: a single candidate is the answer; none is none.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` EMPTY EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A")
-- (2): a Category A (or B) and a Category C (or D) together.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `C pension at 60`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A", "C")
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `B pension at 80`, `D pension at 70`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "B-spouse", "D")
-- (5): no notice, so the most favourable: A at 100 beats B at 80; B at 120 beats A at 100.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 80`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A")
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 120`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "B-widow")
-- (3) and (4): a notice dated before the week begins is obeyed, even for the lower pension.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 80`) (LIST `notice for B-spouse dated 7 January 2024`) `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "B-spouse")
-- (4): "any week commencing after the date of the notice": a notice dated the day the week commences has no effect for that week.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 80`) (LIST `notice for B-spouse dated 8 January 2024`) `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A")
-- (aa): two Category B pensions and no Category A: choose by notice, else the most favourable.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `B pension at 80`, `B pension at 120`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "B-widow")
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `B pension at 80`, `B pension at 120`) (LIST `notice for B-spouse dated 7 January 2024`) `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "B-spouse")
-- (b): a Category C and a Category D.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `C pension at 60`, `D pension at 70`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "D")
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `C pension at 60`, `D pension at 70`) (LIST `notice for C dated 1 January 2024`) `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "C")
-- (2) with (3) in each group: the notice for the Part II group does not disturb the Part III choice.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 80`, `C pension at 60`, `D pension at 70`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A", "D")
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 80`, `C pension at 60`, `D pension at 70`) (LIST `notice for B-spouse dated 7 January 2024`, `notice for C dated 1 January 2024`) `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "B-spouse", "C")
-- A notice naming a pension the person does not have is not "such a notice": the most favourable applies.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 80`) (LIST `notice for a pension nobody has`) `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A")
-- Two notices with effect for the same group: the text does not say which prevails.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `B pension at 80`, `B pension at 120`) (LIST `notice for B-spouse dated 7 January 2024`, `notice for B-widow dated 1 January 2024`) `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Two Category A pensions: the text speaks of one.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `A pension at 20 because of 61ZA`, `B pension at 80`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 61ZC(1): a Category A pension because of s 61ZA together with one Category B pension.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 20 because of 61ZA`, `B pension at 80`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A61", "B-spouse")
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 20 because of 61ZA`, `B pension at 80`, `B pension at 120`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A61", "B-widow")
-- s 61ZC(2): a Category A pension together with one Category B pension because of s 61ZB.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 30 because of 61ZB`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS JUST (LIST "A", "B61")
-- ... beside an ordinary Category B pension the text does not decide (fork F3 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` (LIST `A pension at 100`, `B pension at 30 because of 61ZB`, `B pension at 80`) EMPTY `the week commencing on 8 January 2024` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The regulative rule for the notice (s 43(3)): the person MAY give it, and doing so fulfils the rule.
#TRACE `s 43(3) the person may give notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 43 the person` DOES `s 43 give notice in writing to the Secretary of State specifying which pension is wished to be received` AT 1
#EVAL `s 43(3) the person may give notice`

§ `Section 44: Category A retirement pension`

-- (1A): paragraph 5 for a person attaining pensionable age before 6 April 2010, paragraph 5A on or after that date.
#ASSERT `s 44(1A) the relevant conditions or condition` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2010)) EQUALS `s 44(1A)(a) the conditions specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5`
#ASSERT `s 44(1A) the relevant conditions or condition` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2010)) EQUALS `s 44(1A)(b) the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A`
-- (1): entitled if pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and the relevant conditions are met.
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2016)) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2016)) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2010)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2010)) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2010)) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2012)) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2017)) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1), closing words: the day entitlement begins is the day pensionable age is attained; it continues throughout life.
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the day on which the person becomes entitled` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 9 3 2012)) EQUALS Date 9 3 2012
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the entitlement is running on the day` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 9 3 2012)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 9 3 2012) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the entitlement is running on the day` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 9 3 2012)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 8 3 2012) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the entitlement is running on the day` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 9 3 2012)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 1 2040) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the entitlement is running on the day` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 9 3 2012)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 1 2030) (JUST (Date 1 1 2030)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the entitlement is running on the day` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 9 3 2012)) (JUST TRUE) (Date 2 1 2030) (JUST (Date 1 1 2030)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the entitlement is running on the day` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 9 3 2012)) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 1 2020) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the entitlement is running on the day` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 9 3 2012)) NOTHING (Date 1 1 2020) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): not payable for a period before the day the entitlement is regarded as commencing; the text is silent about the day itself and after.
#ASSERT `s 44(2) the Category A retirement pension is payable in respect of the day` (Date 9 3 2012) (Date 10 3 2012) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(2) the Category A retirement pension is payable in respect of the day` (Date 10 3 2012) (Date 10 3 2012) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(2) the Category A retirement pension is payable in respect of the day` (Date 11 3 2012) (Date 10 3 2012) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the elements.
#ASSERT `s 44(3)(a) the Category A retirement pension consists of a basic pension`
#ASSERT `s 44(3)(b) an additional pension is payable as part of the Category A retirement pension` 1 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(3)(b) an additional pension is payable as part of the Category A retirement pension` 0 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(3)(b) an additional pension is payable as part of the Category A retirement pension` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): the weekly rate of the basic pension is 184.90, but 140.65 for the lower rate of short-term incapacity benefit; "the first 196 days".
#ASSERT `s 44(4) the weekly rate of the basic pension in pounds` FALSE EQUALS JUST 184.90
#ASSERT `s 44(4) the weekly rate of the basic pension in pounds` TRUE EQUALS JUST 140.65
#ASSERT `s 44(4) the day of entitlement is one for which the lower rate is payable` 1
#ASSERT `s 44(4) the day of entitlement is one for which the lower rate is payable` 196
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 44(4) the day of entitlement is one for which the lower rate is payable` 197))
-- (5A): a surplus is an excess over the qualifying earnings factor; its amount; the adjusted amount.
#ASSERT `s 44(5A)(a) there is a surplus in the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` 101 100
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 44(5A)(a) there is a surplus in the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` 100 100))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 44(5A)(a) there is a surplus in the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` 99 100))
#ASSERT `s 44(5A)(b) the amount of the surplus in pounds` 150 100 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 44(5A)(b) the amount of the surplus in pounds` 100 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(5A)(b) the amount of the surplus in pounds` 90 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(5A)(c) the adjusted amount of the surplus in pounds` 50 10 EQUALS 55
#ASSERT `s 44(5A)(c) the adjusted amount of the surplus in pounds` 50 0 EQUALS 50
-- (6): the earnings factor by limb. Limb (za): the first appointed year or later; (a): 1987-88 on, before it; (b): earlier.
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` (`Tax year` OF 2010) TRUE FALSE 5000 1000 700 800 900 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` (`Tax year` OF 1987) FALSE FALSE 5000 1000 700 800 900 EQUALS JUST 1800
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` (`Tax year` OF 1987) FALSE FALSE 5000 1000 700 950 900 EQUALS JUST 1900
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` (`Tax year` OF 1986) FALSE FALSE 5000 1000 700 800 900 EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` (`Tax year` OF 1986) FALSE FALSE 5000 1000 700 950 900 EQUALS JUST 1600
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the pensioner's earnings factor for the relevant year` (`Tax year` OF 2010) TRUE TRUE 5000 1000 700 800 900 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7)(a): relevant years run from the tax year of the sixteenth birthday (inclusive) to the tax year of pensionable age (exclusive), and not before 1978-79.
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 15 8 1990)) (`Tax year` OF 1989) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 15 8 1990)) (`Tax year` OF 1990) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 15 8 1990)) (`Tax year` OF 2014) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 15 8 1990)) (`Tax year` OF 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 1 1 1970)) (`Tax year` OF 1977) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 1 1 1970)) (`Tax year` OF 1978) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- sixteenth birthday on 5 April 1990 falls in the tax year that began in 1989; on 6 April 1990 in the year that began in 1990.
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 5 4 1990)) (`Tax year` OF 1989) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 6 4 1990)) (`Tax year` OF 1989) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- pensionable age on 5 April 2015 is in the year that began in 2014 (exclusive); on 6 April 2015 in the year that began in 2015.
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 5 4 2015)) (JUST (Date 15 8 1990)) (`Tax year` OF 2014) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2015)) (JUST (Date 15 8 1990)) (`Tax year` OF 2014) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(a) the tax year is a relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) NOTHING (`Tax year` OF 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7)(b): the last relevant year is the year before the pensionable-age year, if that is a relevant year at all.
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(b) the final relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) (JUST (Date 15 8 1990)) EQUALS JUST (`Tax year` OF 2014)
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(b) the final relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 7 2015)) (JUST (Date 1 6 2015)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(b) the final relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 7 2015)) (JUST (Date 1 6 2014)) EQUALS JUST (`Tax year` OF 2014)
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(b) the final relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 7 1978)) (JUST (Date 1 1 1950)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(b) the final relevant year` (`a person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 6 2015)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7)(c): the upper earnings limit before 2009-10; the upper accrual point (770) from 2009-10.
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(c) the applicable limit in pounds` (`Earnings limits` OF (`Tax year` OF 2008), 87, 100, 3000, 90) EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(c) the applicable limit in pounds` (`Earnings limits` OF (`Tax year` OF 2009), 95, 110, 3500, 100) EQUALS 770
#ASSERT `s 44(7)(c) the applicable limit in pounds` (`Earnings limits` OF (`Tax year` OF 2020), 120, 200, 9999, 150) EQUALS 770
-- (8): an order under section 21 of the 1975 Act is treated as an order under section 148.
#ASSERT `s 44(8) the order is treated as an order under section 148 of the Administration Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(8) the order is treated as an order under section 148 of the Administration Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
